From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Son Luong Ngoc <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nfsserve: own and drain serving tasks at shutdown

A listener is not the lifetime of its detached connections or nested RPC
workers. Filesystem generations cannot be reclaimed merely by aborting
accept. Add explicit stop-aware serving that owns all spawned work, stops
new task admission, and aborts and joins every worker before returning.
Retain the existing forever-serving API as a compatibility wrapper.
Reap completed workers while serving to keep task ownership bounded.
---
